*Description of problem:*

Following the documentation for creating HCP self-managed on Azure:

* [https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.22/html/hosted_control_planes/deploying-hosted-control-planes#hcp-deploy-azure|https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.22/html/hosted_control_planes/deploying-hosted-control-planes#hcp-deploy-azure]

With the addition of the correction mentioned in doc bug OCPBUGS-98208.

The cluster is installed but the record set *.apps.${CLUSTER_NAME} is created in the parent DNS zone, instead of the DNS zone created for the HCP cluster, in fact following the procedure for "Configuring an Azure management cluster for hosted control planes" steps from 3 to 7 are causing the installation to not complete correctly because the console URL is not resolvable.

*Version-Release number of selected component (if applicable):*

{noformat}4.22{noformat}

*How reproducible:*

{noformat}100% {noformat}

*Steps to Reproduce:*

{noformat}1. Follow the procedure for installing HCP on Azure with the corrections in the doc bug
2. After the installation the console of the HCP cluster is not reachable.
3. Wildcard record set is created in the parent DNS zone.{noformat}

*Actual results:*

{noformat}the record set *.apps.${CLUSTER_NAME} is created in the parent DNS zone, instead of the DNS zone created for the HCP cluster{noformat}

*Expected results:*

{noformat}The record set should be created in the dedicated zone.{noformat}

*Additional info:*

{noformat}{noformat}

